1
00:00:00,119 --> 00:00:02,159
Smoking has been banned on flights for decades,

2
00:00:02,460 --> 00:00:03,980
and there is still an ashtray built into the

3
00:00:04,039 --> 00:00:05,039
airplane bathroom door.

4
00:00:05,299 --> 00:00:06,980
It is not a leftover nobody removed.

5
00:00:07,259 --> 00:00:09,340
Regulators require it, and a plane can be held

6
00:00:09,359 --> 00:00:10,619
on the ground over a broken one.

7
00:00:10,819 --> 00:00:12,719
The reasoning is bleak and completely correct.

8
00:00:13,059 --> 00:00:14,519
Somebody is eventually going to smoke in there

9
00:00:14,559 --> 00:00:16,119
anyway, and the only question is where the

10
00:00:16,180 --> 00:00:16,819
cigarette ends up.

11
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:18,799
Without an ashtray, it goes in the bin,

12
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:20,079
on top of the paper towels.

13
00:00:20,319 --> 00:00:21,520
It is not there for smokers.
